{"content":[{"c":["SHEMER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Owner of the hill of Samaria, which Omri, king of Israel, bought as the site of his new capital city and named after Shemer (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.16.24","r":"1Kgs.16.24","rawR":"1Kgs.16.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.16.24","value":"1Kgs.16.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 16:24"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Merarite Levite, Mahli’s son and the father of Bani; he was a temple singer during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.46","r":"1Chr.6.46","rawR":"1Chr.6.46","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.46","value":"1Chr.6.46"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:46"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Asherite, Heber’s son and a leader among his people (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.34","r":"1Chr.7.34","rawR":"1Chr.7.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.34","value":"1Chr.7.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:34"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Shemer","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 16:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.16.24","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.16.24","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.16.24"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:46","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.46","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.46","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.46"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.34","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.34","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.34"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cfa11b12e508c6e5697e42fd3eb7489a9e9701177dddcc7b433e22770b55cd64","sourceItemName":"Shemer","sourceItemOrder":277,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Shemer","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shemer","title":"She